{
  "id": "corp_04_ice",
  "side": "Corp",
  "title": "Ice and rezzing",
  "intro": "Ice protects a server. It is installed in front of the server, face down, and only stops the Runner once you rez it — which you may do at the moment they approach it, after seeing them commit a click to the run. Palisade is a barrier: its one subroutine ends the run, and it has +2 strength while protecting a remote.\n\nThis lesson: put Palisade in front of your remote, then rez it when the Runner runs.",
  "outro": "You rezzed at the last possible moment, so the Runner spent a click and got nothing. Rezzing costs credits, so keep some in reserve on the Runner's turn. Next: advancing and scoring the agenda the ice is there to protect.",
  "corp_deck": "the_syndicate_starter",
  "runner_deck": "the_catalyst_starter",
